===Agreeing to the favours===
{{Checklist|
*Talk to [[Yanni Salika]] in [[Shilo Village (location)|Shilo Village]] (north of the bridge at the quest icon). {{Chat option|2Is there anything else interesting to do around here?|5Ok, see you in a tick!|1Il'l get going then!}}
*''If mining your own gems, do this now at the [[Shilo Village Mine]].''
*Talk to a [[Jungle forester]] south of Shilo at the tree line (make sure to have 1 free inventory space to receive blunt axe). {{Chat option|1I need to talk to you about red mahogany.|1Ok, I'll take your axe to get it sharpened.}}
*'''Travel tip:''' Use the minigames teleport to Pest Control, then leave by talking to the Squire to the north and you'll be at Port Sarim. Or you Can use the Rat Pits teleport to Port Sarim, if you have completed Rat Catchers.
*Talk to [[Brian]] in the [[Port Sarim]] axe shop. {{Chat option|3Do you sharpen axes?|2Look, can you sharpen this cursed axe or what?|4Ok, ok, I'll do it! I'll go and see Aggie.}}
*Talk to [[Aggie]] in [[Draynor Village]]. {{Chat option|1Can I ask you about being a character witness?|3Let me guess, you're going to ask me to do you a favour?|2Oh, Ok, I'll see if I can find Jimmy.}}
*Talk to [[Johanhus Ulsbrecht]] near the prison inside of the [[H.A.M. Hideout]]. {{Chat option|4I'm looking for Jimmy the Chisel.|3And I suppose you need me to do you a favour?|2Ok, Jimmy has to be worth more than a few scrawny chickens!}}
*Talk to [[Fred the Farmer]] NE of the [[H.A.M. Hideout]] at the [[Sheep Shearer]] quest start point. {{Chat option|3I need to talk to you about Jimmy.}} (4 if you haven't done Sheep Shearer)
*''Prepare a [[bowl of hot water]] and take a pot in the [[Lumbridge Castle]] kitchen if needed.'' Gather 3 steel bars if not already carrying.
*Talk to [[Seth Groats]] in the chicken farm east of [[River Lum]]. {{Chat option|2Oh, ok! I guess it's not that much further to Varrock!}} 
*Talk to [[Horvik]] at the armour shop in [[Varrock]]. Give him 3 steel bars. {{Chat option|3Hi, I need to talk to you about chicken cages!|2Ok, I guess one good turn deserves another.}}
*Talk to the [[Apothecary]] in Varrock south of the western bank. {{Chat option|2Talk about One Small Favour.|2I guess I can go to Barbarian Village.}}
*'''Travel tip:''' [[amulet of glory]] to [[Edgeville]], run south or use a [[skull sceptre]].
*Talk to [[Tassie Slipcast]] in the [[Barbarian Village]] at the pottery icon on the minimap. {{Chat option|1Ok, I'll deal with Hammerspike!}}
*'''Travel tip:''' teleport to the [[Mining Guild]] using a [[skills necklace]].
*Talk to [[Hammerspike Stoutbeard]] in the most western portion of the [[Dwarven Mines]] (SW of the [[Ice Mountain]] entrance). {{Chat option|3Oh, come on...do something nice for Tassie.|4Have you always been a gangster?|2Ok, another favour...I think I can manage that.}}
*''Gather one [[harralander]], two [[guam]] leaves, and one [[marrentill]].''
*'''Travel tip:''' If you have 10 [[Construction]] you can use [[Taverley teleport]]. If you're an ironman without redirect scrolls and have completed [[Enlightened Journey]], [[ring of dueling]] to [[Castle Wars]] and take the [[Balloon Transport System]] to Taverley
*''Pick up the [[cup of tea]] from the house north of [[Sanfew]], then drink the tea to obtain an [[empty cup]], if you haven't got one already.''
*Talk to [[Sanfew]] on the top floor of the [[Taverley]] herblore shop about initiates. {{Chat option|3Are you taking any new initiates?|2Do you accept dwarves?|3A dwarf I know wants to become an initiate.|1Yep, it's a deal.}} (2-2-3-1 if you have completed Eadgar's Ruse)
*Add your bowl of hot water to a teacup. Add a harralander, 2 guam leaves, and a marrentill. The empty bowl can be dropped afterwards.
*'''Travel tip:''' [[Ring of dueling]] to Al Kharid, then use the [[gnome glider]] to White Wolf Mountain.
*Talk to [[Captain Bleemadge]] on top of [[White Wolf Mountain]] at the gnome glider icon on the minimap. {{Chat option|2I have a special tea here for you from Sanfew!|4Ok, I'll go and get you some T.R.A.S.H.}}
*Talk to [[Arhein]] on the Catherby docks south of the bank. {{Chat option|4I need to talk T.R.A.S.H to you.|1Yes, Ok, I'll do it!}}
*Talk to [[Phantuwti Fanstuwi Farsight]] in the building north of the Seers' chapel. {{Chat option|4Hi, can you give me a weather forecast?|5What can I do to help?|1Yes, Ok, I'll do it.}}
*'''Travel tip:''' teleport to the [[Fishing Guild]] using a [[skills necklace]].
*Enter the [[Goblin Cave]] south-east of the Fishing Guild. Go to the most NE room. Right-click and search the sculpture.
*'''Travel tip:''' [[Ardougne Teleport]]
*Talk to [[Wizard Cromperty]] in NE [[Ardougne]] at the transportation icon. {{Chat option|4I need to talk to you about a girl stuck in some rock!|2Oh! Ok, one more 'small favour' isn't going to kill me...I hope!}} ( {{Chat option|2Chat.|4I need to talk to you about a girl stuck in some rock!|2Oh! Ok, one more 'small favour' isn't going to kill me...I hope!}} if you have completed the Ardougne Medium Diary)
*''You can take the hammer and chisel south of Cromperty if you didn't bring your own.''
*'''Travel tip:''' [[Fishing Trawler]] [[Minigame Teleport]]
*Talk to [[Tindel Marchant]] on the [[Port Khazard]] south dock. {{Chat option|2Ask about iron oxide.|1Ok, I'll do it!}}
*''Bring your cut gems, two of each: [[opal]], [[jade]], [[sapphire]], and [[red topaz]] (can be mined with 40 Mining at [[Shilo Village (location)|Shilo Village]]) if you have them, otherwise, bring some gold in case you crush a gem in the upcoming step.'' 
*'''Travel tip:''' [[fairy ring]] teleport ({{fairycode|AKS}}) or [[ring of dueling]] to [[Castle Wars]] and walk east
*Talk to [[Rantz]] in the eastern Feldip Hills at the quest icon on the minimap. {{Chat option|2I need to talk to you about a mattress.|1Can you fill this mattress with feathers?|4Ok, I'll see what I can do.}}
*Talk to [[Gnormadium Avlafrim]] west of Rantz. {{Chat option|4Rantz said I should help you finish this project.|1Yes, I'll take a look at them.}} (at the gnome glider icon on the minimap)
*Search each landing light, cut the gem, and put the cut gem back. If you crush a gem, the gnome will sell you up to 2 new ones for 500 coins.
}}
